OL,3,GNEWSABusinesses blames music festival
OL,4,Afor revenue losses up to #1m
OL,5,
OL,6,FBusinesses in Portsmouth have raised
OL,7,Fconcerns over the impact of an annual
OL,8,Fmusic festival, with one claiming it
OL,9,Fhas lost almost #1m in revenue over the
OL,10,Fpast decade.
OL,12,FPortsmouth City Council heard from
OL,13,Flocal traders during a meeting
OL,14,Fconsidering whether to agree new
OL,15,Fcontracts with Victorious Festival and
OL,16,Fthe Great South Run.
OL,18,FSpeaking to councillors, Jimmy Norman,
OL,19,Fdirector of Clarence Pier, said the
OL,20,Fauthority should "address the impact"
OL,21,Fof Victorious but said he did not want
OL,22,Fto see it leave the city.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
